# PITX2 candidate peaks for per-peak motif scan (§5.7 follow-up).
#
# ⚠ HEADLINE vs EXPLORATORY (2026-06-19).  The locus-FDR candidate TABLE
# (scripts/compute_locus_fdr_h6_h7.py) and molecular_model §8.7.12 report ONLY
# the headline set — peaks with a standing basis: Peak_1 (PITX2c promoter,
# a-priori), Peak_3 (+5.4 kb, independent motif basis per fig04), and
# PITX2a_promoter (bilateral within-locus control).  ASE_region, SMAD5plus,
# Peak_2, Peak_4 and Peak_5 are RETIRED FROM THE HEADLINE (significance-driven /
# since-reframed selection — ASE's Welsh citation retracted; SMAD5 shown to be a
# broad-domain property, not a focal BRE; Peak_2 reframed as gene-body — see
# docs/pitx2_locus_window_rationale.md, not distributed).  They stay in THIS file only so the
# exploratory motif / co-accessibility / gkm-SVM scans that documented their
# weakness still reproduce; do not present them as candidates.
#
# These are the 6 candidate peaks downstream of Peak #1 in the §5 chromatin-
# laterality narrative (Peak #1 is the PITX2c proximal promoter, already
# covered by references/pitx2_promoter_regions.bed as promoter|PITX2c and
# scanned in g3_pitx2_motif_scan_p5e-3.tsv).  Coordinates are NC_051775.1,
# zju1, 0-based half-open (BED convention).
#
# Source of coordinates:
#   - Peak #2..#5 + PITX2a promoter peak + SMAD5+ composite all appear as
#     rows in figures/data/h0_lvr_peaks_pitx2_locus.tsv (h0 = 329 peaks
#     within PITX2 ±500 kb on NC_051775.1, derived from ArchR pseudobulk).
#   - Candidate-peak short labels match the CANDIDATE_PEAKS list of the
#     co-accessibility script (not distributed), which is the §5.4 co-accessibility
#     consumer.
#
# Peak descriptions (relative to PITX2c TSS at 3,971,385):
#   Peak #2     +599 bp   over PITX2c exon 1 CDS (§8.7.2 chick synteny)
#   Peak #3     +5.4 kb   intragenic, PITX+SMAD2/3 motif hits in h0
#   Peak #4     +552 kb   far 3' distal
#   Peak #5     -2.06 Mb  far 5' distal
#   SMAD5+     +11.0 kb  composite peak (was previously labeled "+6 kb" in
#                          docs/h1; the analytical position has been
#                          NC_051775.1:3,982,405-3,982,906 = +11 kb 3' of
#                          PITX2c TSS at 3,971,385 since all g3b/h2/h6/h7
#                          DESeq2 + motif analyses ran on this coord)
#                          NAME CAVEAT (2026-06-16): "SMAD5plus" is a legacy
#                          landmark label from a curated SMAD5-PWM (MA1557.1)
#                          *presence* call — NOT a validated SMAD/BMP footprint.
#                          The focal footprint/occupancy probe found 0 direct
#                          SMAD at this locus (SMAD5 ~ background; BMP
#                          indirect); the cross-species BRE scan (g3d) finds
#                          this window's BRE at chance rate
#                          (1 of 5 scattered non-specific windows); the de-novo
#                          "SMAD5" motif enrichment was a retracted attribution
#                          artefact (GTCT core = NODAL SBE, not the BMP
#                          GC-rich BRE). Name
#                          retained as a coordinate landmark only (cf. the
#                          ASE_region precedent below); it does NOT assert
#                          SMAD/BMP function.
#   PITX2a_promoter  -10 kb 5'   over PITX2a TSS at 3,961,387
#   ASE_region  +3.0 kb   syntenic-position to a chick PITX2c last-intron
#                          "ASE region" cited in our internal docs.
#                          PRIMARY CITATION PENDING — was originally
#                          attributed to Welsh et al. 2015 (PMID 26411685)
#                          but that paper is about CTCF + Playrr-mediated
#                          chromatin asymmetry, NOT a PITX2c last-intron
#                          ASE or FoxH1 binding. Verified against PubMed
#                          on 2026-05-22. The position 3974421-3974922
#                          was chosen for motif-conservation testing;
#                          the substantive scan result (0/0/2 FoxH1 hits
#                          at p<5e-4 / 5e-3 / 1e-2, contrasted with
#                          Peak #4 at 6/10 hits) is independent of the
#                          motivating citation. raw-significant L-biased
#                          peak from h0 (log2FC=+1.05, raw binom_p=0.003,
#                          padj=0.74 at genome-wide 283K-burden FDR;
#                          locus padj 0.043 at HH25 h7 unpaired —
#                          newly emerging).
#
# Peak #1 (PITX2c proximal promoter) IS included even though g3 already
# scanned the 601-bp `promoter|PITX2c` BED region containing it — we
# want apples-to-apples comparison across all 7 peaks at the same
# 501-bp window AND with the same 27-motif catalog (g3 used 21 motifs;
# g3b adds MEIS1/2/3 + PBX1/2/3).
#
# chrom        start      end       name              score  strand
NC_051775.1	3971182	3971683	Peak_1	0	+
NC_051775.1	3971734	3972235	Peak_2	0	+
NC_051775.1	3976533	3977034	Peak_3	0	+
